      "rev_n_3_0ff2f0_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_0ff2f0_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_0ff2f0",
        "thought_text": "The code incorrectly identifies a sequence ending at 15 as \"UP\" because it only checks for strict monotonicity without verifying if the last element is the cycle's peak (15) or valley (0), which forces a direction change regardless of the previous trend. The corrected logic must explicitly check if the last element is 15 (output \"DOWN\") or 0 (output \"UP\") before evaluating the general increasing/decreasing pattern.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_0ff2f0_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_7e425b375d",
        "created_at": 1794508877.9450254
      },
      "rev_n_4_8e3177_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_8e3177_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_8e3177",
        "thought_text": "Check if the sequence ends at the peak (15) or valley (0/1) to determine a forced direction, otherwise check if the sequence is strictly increasing or decreasing within the cycle bounds to predict the next step.",
